  21:  *     `textContent`, which is precisely and only what `esc()` uses it for;
  22:  *   - `getElementById` hands back a fake `#terr-root` whose `innerHTML` we can
  23:  *     read, plus fake modal fields for the submit handler.
  24:  *
  25:  * That is enough to drive the REAL functions and assert on the REAL rendered
  26:  * markup and the REAL persisted payload. Only the CSS-file assertions at the
  27:  * bottom are static, because a stylesheet has no behaviour to exercise.
