  12: # Story TBID.1: Territory Bids — open-flow board, resolved-collapse, wipe, CSS/token cleanup
  13: 
  14: ## Story
  15: 
  16: As the Storyteller running a live session,
  17: I want the Territory Bids board to start empty and let me open a bid for one specific territory —
  18: picking which territory, then confirming its Regent — instead of always showing all five,
  19: so that the board reflects only what's actually being contested right now, resolved territories
  20: stay visible as a compact record I can point back to, and I have a guarded way to clear the whole
  21: board for a fresh session.
  22: 
  23: ## Why this story exists
  24: 
  25: Angelus asked for this directly (2026-08-28 session), then it was worked through in a two-round
  26: `bmad-party-mode` discussion (Sally/UX, Winston/Architect, Amelia/Dev) before being scoped here.
  27: There is no epic doc for this tool — `public/js/suite/territory.js` (the "Territory Bids" tab) is
  28: a standalone, client-only, localStorage-backed ST scratchpad for adjudicating the five city
  29: territories' bidding at the table. It has never been epic-tracked in this repo (confirmed: no
  30: `epic-terr*.md`, no prior `sprint-status.yaml` row for this file). It is unrelated to the
  31: DB-backed `server/routes/territories.js` API (regent/lieutenant/feeding-rights) — this story does
  32: not touch that route or its schema at all.
  33: 
  34: Two decisions were explicitly made by Angelus during the discussion and are LOCKED, not proposals
  35: to re-litigate:
  36: 
  37: - **Resolved territories stay on the board** (do not clear back to the picker).
  38: - **A "wipe the board" action must exist, gated behind a confirmation.**
  39: 
  40: Two further decisions were left as open questions during the discussion and were confirmed by
  41: Angelus in the same session — also LOCKED:
  42: 
  43: - **State model:** `state.territories` becomes an empty-startable array (`[]` by default), not the
  44:   always-five array it is today. A `schemaVersion` field on the persisted payload grandfathers in
  45:   any pre-existing populated `tm_bids_v2` save so a live in-progress board isn't wiped by this
  46:   deploy (see AC5/AC6).
  47: - **Wipe-board confirm wording:** static, matching this file's own existing `confirm()` idiom
  48:   (`terrRmBid` already uses one) — not a dynamic N/M-territory count.
  49: 
  50: ## Decisions already made (do not re-litigate)
  51: 
  52: - **The picker is a two-beat sequence inside the existing modal system, not a combined form.**
  53:   Step 1: a grid of the five static `TERRS` tiles (name + ambience modifier), already-open
  54:   territories shown disabled/greyed with an "In Contest" label — **not removed from the list**.
  55:   Step 2 (after clicking an available tile): the same modal transforms in place to a Regent-confirm
  56:   step, the territory's `defaultRegent` pre-selected, overridable via the same name-select pattern
  57:   (`nameOpts()`) already used elsewhere in this file. Confirming is what actually adds the card to
  58:   `state.territories` — picking a territory alone does not.
  59: - **Reopening a resolved territory re-enters the same Regent-confirm step (step 2 above)**, not a
  60:   blind re-arm — pre-filling the previous winner as the default, overridable, because a reopened
  61:   territory may have a genuinely different contested Regent this time.
  62: - **`state.phase` (`'open' | 'final' | 'reveal'`) is a single GLOBAL field, not per-territory** —
  63:   confirmed by reading the current code: no action function (`terrAddBid`, `terrResolve`,
  64:   `terrAddBack`, etc.) reads or branches on `state.phase` at all; only the toolbar's own
  65:   `terrAdvance`/`terrBack` buttons touch it, purely as a display label. This resolves the one open
  66:   question from the design discussion: a newly-opened territory needs no phase-aware special-casing
  67:   — it just renders normally under whatever the current global phase is, exactly like every other
  68:   territory does today.
  69: - **The existing in-card Regent `<select>`** (`.regent-row`, wired to `window.terrSetRegent`) is
  70:   UNCHANGED and stays — it becomes a post-open override on the `regent` field the open-flow set,
  71:   not a replacement for it. Nobody in the discussion asked for its removal.
  72: - **`terrAddBid`'s existing auto-regent-defence-bid logic is unchanged** — it already guards on
  73:   `t.regent` being truthy, and `regent` will now always be non-empty by the time a territory exists
  74:   on the board (the open-flow requires confirming one before the card is created), so this keeps
  75:   working with zero code changes to that function.
  76: - **`.form-select`/`.form-input` (in `public/css/components.css:40-44`) already exist** as shared,
  77:   token-based classes — confirmed by grep before scoping this story. The modal's `selStyle` inline
  78:   string (territory.js:368-386) is replaced by applying these EXISTING classes to the four modal
  79:   fields; no new CSS class is needed for that part.
  80: - **Naming collision avoided on purpose:** the existing `window.terrOpenBidModal(tid, tname)`
  81:   (opens the claimant/seconder bid modal for an ALREADY-open territory card) is NOT renamed and NOT
  82:   reused for the new picker entry point — a new, distinctly-named function
  83:   (`window.terrOpenTerritoryPicker()`, see Dev Notes) is added instead. Reusing the old name for
  84:   the new picker would silently shadow the existing per-territory "add a bid" flow.
  85: 
  86: ## Acceptance Criteria
  87: 
  88: 1. **On a fresh `tm_bids_v2` (no existing save), the board renders with zero territory cards.** A
  89:    visible "Open Territory Bid" control is present in the toolbar regardless of board state (empty
  90:    or populated) — it is not conditionally hidden.
  91: 2. **`state.territories` defaults to `[]`.** `dflt()` (territory.js:33-39) no longer maps `TERRS`
  92:    into `state.territories` — `TERRS` itself is UNCHANGED and stays the static 5-entry catalogue
  93:    (id, name, defaultRegent, ambience, ambienceMod), now consumed only by the picker.
  94: 3. **Clicking "Open Territory Bid" opens step 1 of the picker**: a grid of the five `TERRS`
  95:    entries. A territory already present in `state.territories` (in ANY status — active/in-bidding
  96:    or resolved) renders disabled, visually greyed, labelled "In Contest" — present, not hidden.
  97: 4. **Clicking an available (non-disabled) tile advances to step 2**, in the same modal: a
  98:    Regent-confirm field, pre-selected to that territory's `defaultRegent`, overridable via
  99:    `nameOpts()`. Confirming:
 100:    - Pushes a new entry onto `state.territories`: `{ ...territoryDef, regent: <confirmed>,
 101:      regentInput: <confirmed>, bids: [], resolved: false, winnerId: null }` (mirrors the shape
 102:      `dflt()`'s old per-territory object already used).
 103:    - Closes the modal, persists, re-renders.
 104: 5. **Existing populated `tm_bids_v2` saves are not wiped by this deploy.** On `load()`
 105:    (territory.js:41-47): if the parsed payload has `schemaVersion` absent AND a non-empty
 106:    `territories` array, treat it as pre-existing state from before this story — keep its
 107:    territories exactly as saved (do not reset to `[]`), and stamp `schemaVersion: 1` into it before
 108:    the next `persist()`. A payload with `schemaVersion` already present, or with an empty/absent
 109:    `territories` array, uses the new `dflt()` (`[]`) unchanged.
 110: 6. **`persist()` (territory.js:49-60) writes `schemaVersion: 1`** alongside the existing
 111:    `phase`/`peek`/`territories` fields on every save going forward.
 112: 7. **A resolved territory (`t.resolved === true`) stays in `state.territories` and renders as a
 113:    compact collapsed row**, not the full bid card: territory name, the winning Regent's name, a
 114:    "Resolved" tag, and a low-emphasis "Reopen" link/button. It does NOT show bid amounts or the
 115:    challenger list by default.
 116: 8. **Clicking "Reopen" on a resolved row re-enters the Regent-confirm step (AC4's step 2)** for
 117:    that same territory, pre-filling the previous winner (`t.winnerId`'s claimant, or `t.regent`) as
 118:    the default, overridable. Confirming resets that entry's `bids: []`, `resolved: false`,
 119:    `winnerId: null`, and updates `regent`/`regentInput` — it does NOT remove and re-add the entry
 120:    (same object, same position).
 121: 9. **The existing "Reset All" button is renamed "Wipe Board" and only renders once
 122:    `state.territories.length > 0`.** Clicking it prompts
 123:    `confirm('Wipe the entire board? This removes all territories and bids.')` (static wording, no
 124:    dynamic count). On confirm: `state.territories` resets to `[]` — `phase`/`peek` reset the same
 125:    way `terrResetAll` already does today (via `dflt()`). On cancel: no state change.
 126:    `window.terrResetAll`'s existing regent/regentInput carry-over merge logic (territory.js:115-127)
 127:    becomes dead code under the new empty-start model (there is nothing to merge into an empty
 128:    array) and should be deleted, not kept as an unreachable branch.
 129: 10. **`territory.js:331`'s `var(--text3)` is fixed to `var(--txt3)`** — confirmed via
 130:     `public/css/theme.css:43,305` that `--txt3` is the real token and `--text3` does not exist
 131:     anywhere in the codebase. Per AC11 below this fix is delivered by moving the rule into a CSS
 132:     class rather than patching the inline string in place.
 133: 11. **Every inline `style="..."` attribute in `territory.js` is removed**, replaced by classes:
 134:     - Lines 320/322 (`.tc-foot`'s two footer buttons, `style="flex:1"`): add
 135:       `#t-territory .tc-foot button{flex:1}` to `suite.css` (the `.tc-foot` container already
 136:       exists at suite.css:545); delete both inline attributes, no new class name needed on the
 137:       buttons themselves.
 138:     - Line 258 (ruler-adjust Reset button, `style="padding:3px 8px;margin-left:4px"`): add a scoped
 139:       rule, e.g. `#t-territory .ruler-row .btn-sm{padding:3px 8px;margin-left:4px}`, to `suite.css`
 140:       (`.ruler-row` container already exists at suite.css around the ruler block); delete the
 141:       inline attribute.
 142:     - Line 331 (Reopen button/link, `style="color:var(--text3);border-color:var(--text3)"`): add
 143:       `#t-territory .res-bar .btn-sm{color:var(--txt3);border-color:var(--txt3)}` to `suite.css`
 144:       (`.res-bar` already exists at suite.css:546); delete the inline attribute. This is the same
 145:       change as AC10 — one class addition satisfies both.
 146:     - Lines 368-386 (the `selStyle` string, 4 modal fields): delete `selStyle` entirely; apply the
 147:       EXISTING `.form-select` class (for the two `<select>` fields — claimant, seconder, player,
 148:       territory-picker fields) and `.form-input` class (for the influence-amount `<input>`) from
 149:       `public/css/components.css:40-44`. No new CSS needed for this part.
 150:     - All colour/spacing/font values added under this AC must be existing `theme.css` tokens —
 151:       no new hex or `rgba(...)` literal anywhere (matches this repo's own standing CSS rule,
 152:       `specs/project-context.md`).
 153: 12. **New UI introduced by this story (the territory-tile grid, the disabled/"In Contest" tile
 154:     state, the collapsed resolved row, the empty-board hint state) is styled with new, scoped
 155:     `#t-territory`-prefixed classes in `suite.css`, built entirely from existing `theme.css`
 156:     tokens** — reusing the existing `.overlay`/`.modal`/`.modal-title`/`.modal-sub`/`.field`/
 157:     `.modal-err`/`.modal-btns` chrome already defined for the current bid/back modal (territory.js
 158:     already renders these via `renderModal()`) for the picker's own modal shell. The empty-board
 159:     hint may follow `.no-bids-msg`'s existing pattern (`suite.css:491`, token-only, no new
 160:     literals) as its closest precedent, though it needs its own container.
 161: 13. **No changes to `server/routes/territories.js`, its schema, or any DB-backed territory data.**
 162:     This story is scoped entirely to `public/js/suite/territory.js` and the `#t-territory` block of
 163:     `public/css/suite.css`.
 164: 
 165: ## What this story is NOT
 166: 
 167: - **Does NOT touch the DB-backed territory API** (`server/routes/territories.js` —
 168:   regent/lieutenant/feeding-rights) or the `territories` MongoDB collection in any way. That route
 169:   has its own separate `regent_id`/`lieutenant_id`/`feeding_rights` concept entirely unrelated to
 170:   this localStorage tool's own `regent` string field.
 171: - **Does NOT change scoring/resolution logic.** `total()`, `terrResolve`'s highest-score-wins logic,
 172:   the regent's automatic +3 defence bid, and the "Prince's Peek" fuzzing toggle are all UNCHANGED.
 173: - **Does NOT add multi-device or server sync for this tool.** State remains single-browser
 174:   localStorage (`tm_bids_v2`), same as today — this story only changes what's stored and rendered
 175:   within that same persistence model.
 176: - **Does NOT rework `renderBid`/`renderCard`'s internals for an already-open, unresolved territory**
 177:   beyond what AC11/AC12 requires — the in-progress bid card (claimant list, backing, ruler
 178:   adjustment) keeps its current full-detail rendering; only the RESOLVED state gets a new collapsed
 179:   presentation (AC7).
 180: - **Does NOT add a way to remove an active (non-resolved) territory from the board individually.**

